# Promises
Never promise a dying person you'll stay|They hold you to it|A granddaughter promises her dying grandmother she'll stay until morning; she leaves for an hour, and the grandmother is still waiting when she returns.|GRANDDAUGHTER; GRANDMOTHER; NURSE|A hospital room at night|She needed to go home|The grandmother died at the moment she promised, and she hasn't left|The empty bed, the grandmother's hand, the granddaughter's coat|debt|sad
Don't make a promise in the rain|The rain remembers|A man promises his wife he'll change during a rainstorm; every time it rains, she asks him to keep the promise again.|HUSBAND; WIFE; THE RAIN|A rooftop during the first rain|He wanted to comfort her|The rain repeats the promise every time it falls|The rain, the wife at the window, the husband silent|witness|sad
