Don't promise a child a gift you can't give|The child keeps waiting|An uncle promises his niece a bicycle; he doesn't buy it, and every birthday she waits at the gate.|UNCLE; NIECE; SISTER|A veranda with a gate|He wanted to make her happy|The niece is still waiting as an adult|The gate, the empty road, the niece's hands|invitation|sad
Never promise to return if you won't|Your return is arranged|A traveler promises his mother he'll return for Eid; he dies on the way, and on Eid a man with his face knocks at the door.|TRAVELER; MOTHER; THE MAN|A bus station at Eid|He wanted to ease her mind|The man is the traveler, with no memory of the road|The door, the mother's smile, the traveler's bag|mimicry|sad
